  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds an Aura3D orrery with an emissive star at the centre and a bloom effect. A point light at the star lights the planets, on a near-black background. Five planets of different sizes and colours orbit at radii 3.6 to 11 and at different speeds, and the outermost planet has a tilted torus ring that follows it. Faint torus guides mark the orbits. The camera is at [0, 14, 17] looking at the origin, which should frame all the orbits. The code sets `window.__EVAL_READY__` one animation frame after the first update. `typecheck` passes. I couldn't run `vite build` or view the render, so the look is untested. That includes the torus orientation, the ring tilt and the point-light brightness (intensity 400), which I chose from the docs and may need tuning.",
